---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Support YEGFacts"
  description="How to support the research and operating costs behind YEGFacts, and the funding policy that comes with it."
>
  <header class="border-b border-rule pb-6">
    <h1 class="text-[1.75rem] leading-[1.15] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.022em] sm:text-display">
      Support YEGFacts
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Checking a claim properly costs time and money: reading council reports, chasing records that
      are not posted anywhere, archiving every cited source and checking each published statement
      back against those archived bytes at the publication gate. Contributions pay for that work and
      for keeping the site running.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-9">
    <div class="border border-rule-strong bg-wash px-4 py-5">
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-forest">Contribution links coming soon</h2>
      <p class="mt-1.5 max-w-prose text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Payment links are not live yet. Until they are, the most useful support is evidence and
        corrections: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-navy underline">{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.015em] text-forest">
      What your money does and does not buy
    </h2>
    <p>
      Contributions support research and operating costs. They buy no editorial influence of any
      kind: not which claims get checked, not how a claim is framed, and certainly not what the
      finding turns out to be. There is no tier that comes with a say.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contributions are disclosed. Anyone who contributes materially is named on this page unless
      they ask not to be, in which case the amount is still disclosed without the name.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nobody who is a subject of a check — a candidate, a party, a campaign, or a firm holding a
      City contract we are examining — can contribute. If a contribution like that arrives, it is
      returned and the fact is recorded here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.015em] text-forest">
      These are not charitable donations
    </h2>
    <p>
      Being plain about this: YEGFacts is operated as a for-profit business, not a registered
      charity. Contributions are <strong class="font-semibold">not charitable donations</strong>,
      they are not tax-deductible, and{' '}
      <strong class="font-semibold">no tax receipt is issued</strong>. If you are contributing
      because you want a receipt, this is not that.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.015em] text-forest">Why this is credible</h2>
    <p>
      Independence claims are cheap. What makes this one checkable is that the whole process is in
      public: the evidence behind every finding, what each of the three models concluded and where
      they disagreed, the rule that combined those verdicts, and a dated history of every revision.
      My role is applying that published methodology — published changes are inspectable in the
      version-controlled history, sitting next to the evidence they touch. See{' '}
      <a href="/methodology" class="text-navy underline">the methodology</a> and{' '}
      <a href="/about" class="text-navy underline">about &amp; independence</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
